"<!-- ds:init start. Written by \`ds init\`. A new run replaces the text up to the end marker. -->

# Design: The system

Framework: React with Next.js. System source: the \`@the-system/*\` packages.

## Setup

In the root layout, the system CSS first, then the app CSS. Stamp the theme on \`<html>\` on the server so the first paint is themed:

\`\`\`tsx
import '@the-system/tokens/css';
import '@the-system/css';
import '@the-system/styles';
import './app.css';
import { Theme, Toaster, themeAttributes } from '@the-system/react';

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html {...themeAttributes({ style: 'studio', scheme: 'dark', lang: 'en' })}>
      <body>
        <Theme style="studio" scheme="dark" lang="en">
          <Toaster />
          {children}
        </Theme>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
\`\`\`

The packages export TypeScript and CSS source, so list them in \`transpilePackages\` in \`next.config.ts\`:

\`\`\`ts
transpilePackages: ['@the-system/react', '@the-system/shared', '@the-system/icons', '@the-system/motion', '@the-system/styles', '@the-system/css', '@the-system/tokens'],
\`\`\`

## Theme axes

Set them on the one root theme. Nested themes may change any axis for a part of the page.

| Axis | Values |
| --- | --- |
| style | \`desk\`, \`liquid\`, \`neutral\`, \`studio\` (\`npx ds style list\`) |
| scheme | \`dark\`, \`light\` |
| density | \`compact\`, \`default\`, \`comfortable\` |
| contrast | \`default\`, \`more\` |
| platform | \`web\`, \`ios\`, \`android\` |
| dir, lang | \`ltr\` or \`rtl\`, \`en\` or \`ar\` |

## Where to look

- \`/llms.txt\` on the docs site root: every component, for agents. \`/llms-full.txt\` has the full text.
- \`npx ds docs <Name>\` and \`npx ds manifest <Name>\`: one component, from its manifest.
- \`npx ds doctor\`: checks this app against the rules in AGENTS.md.

<!-- ds:init end -->
"
`;

